    "id": "rate_half_ca_hankel_a1_core_one_exceptional_only_distance_three_quartic_support_laurent_gcd_exclusion",
    "title": "Rate-half distance-three quartic support Laurent gcd exclusion",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "proof using the Corvaja--Zannier positive-characteristic gcd theorem",
    "statement": "The absolutely irreducible Laurent-end quartic curve cannot contain the required e-148 matched fibers. On its normalization deg x=deg y=3, genus is at most 4, and chi is at most 18; the Corvaja--Zannier gcd theorem applied to x^N,y^N gives a bound below 2(e-148) for both its cube-root and characteristic terms. Hence only bounded-tail dihedral matching and cyclic/dihedral quartic pullbacks remain.",
